  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of non-ionisable protons present in the product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> obtained from the following reaction is___<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math></p><p>A is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>(<em>Phosphorous acid</em>)</p><p>The basicity of A is two</p><p>B is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>(Pyrophosphorous acid)</p><p>Structure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is as given below</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0061_f83be45eb218.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 100px;\" /></p><p>Hydrogen&nbsp;which are directly attached to the phosphorous in the above structure are&nbsp;non-ionisable.</p><p>The Number&nbsp;of non-ionisable hydrogen atoms are two in the above structure.</p></blockquote>"
